2026-09-25 02:29 llm-advisor 2026-09-25, docs only, no live call. Sources: docs.perplexity.ai/docs/agent-api/tools/custom-functions.md, .../building-agents/give-it-tools.md, api-reference/agent-post.md (OpenAPI for POST /v1/agent), all fetched 2026-09-25.
CONFIRMED: type:function tools are CLIENT-executed ('the Agent API never executes it for you'). The response output[] has a top-level {type:function_call, id:'fc_…', call_id, name, arguments:<JSON string>, status, thought_signature?}. The client sends back input items {type:function_call_output, call_id, output:<string | [input_text/input_image parts]>}. Request FunctionTool = {type:function, name, description?, parameters?, strict?} (flat, the same as the responses wire). The CLAUDE.md/POD claim 'NO tool calling' is stale for /v1/agent.
tool_choice: NOT in the ResponsesRequest schema, and there is no parallel_tool_calls either. Top-level fields: input, background, instructions, language_preference, max_output_tokens, max_steps, model, models, preset, profile, previous_response_id, reasoning, response_format, store, stream, tools, skills, temperature, top_p. So clear every tool_choice_* flag and keep parallel_tool_use off. Upside: with tool_choice_named cleared, the ADR 0005 direction-1 rewrite (forced tool -> json_schema + synthetic ToolCall) still fires, and Perplexity KEEPS its exemplar role.
SHOWSTOPPER FOR THE ECHO: InputItem is a closed oneOf of message | function_call | function_call_output. InputContentPart.type is only input_text | input_image. Role::Tools format_tool_results('responses') echoes ALL of output[] verbatim. On Perplexity that includes search_results / fetch_url_results / finance_results / sandbox_results / mcp_* items, and assistant message items whose parts are output_text. All of those are off-schema as input and will likely 400 (unverified live). Perplexity's own TS sample replays only the function_call items (keeping thought_signature) plus function_call_output.
WHAT LANGERTHA NEEDS: (1) Perplexity composes Role::Tools. tool_wire_format 'responses' comes from ResponsesCompatible's builder, so apply the -excludes canon on _build_tool_wire_format per ADR 0015. No ParallelToolUse. (2) around engine_capabilities: delete tool_choice_auto/any/none/named. ResponsesCompatible::chat_request must stop emitting tool_choice when !supports (today it emits it whenever it is passed). (3) A sixth ResponsesCompatible divergence hook, e.g. _responses_echo_item($item) -> item|(), called from Role::Tools' responses branch. The default passes through. Perplexity keeps function_call (with thought_signature), turns an assistant message into {type:message, role:assistant, content:<text string>}, and drops every *_results / mcp_* item. This is the ADR 0020 hook shape. It is not per-format code on the engine (ADR 0001). (4) Inbound: chat_response already lifts top-level function_call -> Response.tool_calls. Nothing to do there. (5) Streaming depends on k212. Keep streaming+tools off or croak until then. (6) Presets MERGE tools per tool (presets.md: 'tools are the one exception: they merge'), so a function tool coexists with the preset's web_search in one turn. The echo filter in (3) is therefore needed on the very first tool turn.
FIT WITH SPEC (2026-09-25-server-side-tools-design.md): client function tools do NOT need the ServerTool seam. They are the existing Tool/ToolCall/ToolResult 'responses' path, so ship them as a standalone k213 change. It can land before k206 Phase 1. The built-in tools (web_search, fetch_url, sandbox, people_search, finance_search, mcp) are the part that belongs in the spec as its Phase 2 'Perplexity' bullet: recognizer table, *_results -> server_tool_calls/citations, echo filter shared with (3). Needs the maintainer's OK for 2 captures: a function_call turn, and its echo turn with a preset (web_search present).
SIDE DRIFT: Perplexity now also runs a 'Router' gateway (api-reference gateway-chat-completions-post / gateway-responses-post / gateway-messages-post, with Bearer or x-api-key). It is a separate, OpenAI/Anthropic-shaped surface. Not in scope here. Noted for a later engine decision.

